// =============================================================================
// EXAMPLE AGENTS LAYER — configuration for AI coding agents
// =============================================================================
//
// Copy this folder, with seccomp-bwrap.json, to
// ~/.config/dctl/devcontainer/agents/. It adds what agent CLIs (Claude Code,
// Codex CLI, Gemini CLI) need inside a dctl container:
//
//   1. Mounts for each agent's config directory, so auth and history persist
//      across container recreations.
//   2. `runArgs` that let agents use bubblewrap (`bwrap`) for an internal
//      sandbox, primarily OpenAI Codex CLI, while a syscall filter still
//      applies to the container.
//
// The image of the user installs the agent CLIs. This layer installs nothing.
//
// WHAT EACH runArg DOES
// ---------------------
//   --security-opt seccomp=<path>/seccomp-bwrap.json
//       A default-allow syscall filter with explicit EPERM denies on the
//       syscalls most often used in container escape and kernel privilege
//       escalation (bpf, userfaultfd, perf_event_open, keyctl, kexec_*,
//       init_module, and others). Stronger than seccomp=unconfined, and
//       looser than moby's default profile, so bubblewrap, build tools,
//       `strace`, and `gdb` keep working. The `_meta` block of the file
//       holds its design notes and references.
//
//   --security-opt apparmor=unconfined
//       Loads no AppArmor profile for this container. Ubuntu 23.10 and later
//       deny `unshare` of user namespaces through AppArmor.
//
//   --security-opt systempaths=unconfined
//       Does not mask /proc/sys and similar paths. bwrap reads some of them
//       to probe kernel support for user namespaces.
//
// These flags grant no extra capability: no `--privileged`, no CAP_SYS_ADMIN,
// and the same non-root user.
//
// SECCOMP PROFILE PATH
// --------------------
// The devcontainer CLI resolves the path under runArgs on the host. The
// literal path assumes that XDG_CONFIG_HOME is ~/.config. With another value,
// override `runArgs` in your leaf layer. If the file is missing, the container
// fails to start: there is no fallback to seccomp=unconfined.
//
// REFERENCES
// ----------
//   https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/seccomp/
//   https://github.com/moby/profiles/blob/main/seccomp/default.json
//   https://developers.openai.com/codex/concepts/sandboxing
//   https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap
//
// =============================================================================
{
  "runArgs": [
    "--security-opt", "seccomp=${localEnv:HOME}/.config/dctl/devcontainer/agents/seccomp-bwrap.json",
    "--security-opt", "apparmor=unconfined",
    "--security-opt", "systempaths=unconfined"
  ],
  "mounts": [
    {
      "source": "${localEnv:HOME}/.claude",
      "target": "${localEnv:HOME}/.claude",
      "type": "bind"
    },
    {
      "source": "${localEnv:HOME}/.claude.json",
      "target": "${localEnv:HOME}/.claude.json",
      "type": "bind"
    },
    {
      "source": "${localEnv:HOME}/.codex",
      "target": "${localEnv:HOME}/.codex",
      "type": "bind"
    },
    {
      "source": "${localEnv:HOME}/.gemini",
      "target": "${localEnv:HOME}/.gemini",
      "type": "bind"
    }
  ]
}
